@bank all
// SW3 (2026-10-26, Pillar 5 Step 5; plans/p5-step5-spec.html on claude/p5-specs, "The beats" and section 10): the crew's
// talk around the Senior Officer promotion, for 24u's puTalkTick (modelled on 24p's promoTalkTick: one bubble from
// someone near you, each person once a beat a day; the Works bay and meals, the evening's talk anywhere). Kinds mirror
// the first promotion's pb.* (content/banks/promo-beats.lines): pu3.soon (from the offer: how fast, by days aboard),
// pu3.luck (friends: the evening before and the test morning; also the chat card), pu3.watch (you at the test, in the bay
// or on Deck 6), pu3.passed (the test done, the result not yet given; the bay that evening), pu3.senior (the day you're
// made Senior Officer), pu3.bar.friend (friends right after the bar), pu3.cake (two friends at Brennan's cake),
// pu3.warned (one of the two people you warn in the test: their answer). Spoken over heads: 60 characters or fewer.
// You are "you" or {nick}; never a guess at your pronouns.

== pu3.soon
? day:-14
- Tier 3 already? You've been aboard two weeks.
- Two weeks aboard and up for Senior. Calder means it.
- A Tier 3 test inside a fortnight. That's not normal.
? day:-14 dept:works
- Two weeks and up for Tier 3. Took me two years.   #funny
- Tier 3 at two weeks. I'm telling the night crew.
? day:15-
- Up for Tier 3, I hear. That came round quick.
- Senior Officer's test, then. Good. You've earned it.
?
- Heard you're up for Tier 3. A shutdown, isn't it?
- Calder put you up for Senior? She doesn't do that lightly.
- A Tier 3 test after the storm you had. Fair enough.
- Tier 3 means you switch things off. On purpose.   #funny
? dept:works
- Tier 3 is a junction shutdown. Warn people first.
- Your Tier 3's a junction. Rubber gloves, mind.
- It's always the port junction on Deck 6. Always.   #funny
? act:breakfast|dinner
- So you're the one up for Tier 3. Everyone's saying.
- Eat up. Senior test tomorrow, I hear.

== pu3.luck
? tier>=friend
- Good luck tomorrow. You did the storm. This is nothing.   #warm
- Big day tomorrow. Early night, all right?   #warm
- Tier 3 tomorrow. I've got a cup up for you.   #warm
- To your test. Cheers. No, really, cheers.   #funny
? tier>=friend time:morning
- Today's the day. Go and switch something off.   #funny
- Good luck. Warn everyone twice. You'll be fine.   #warm
- Eat something first. Shutdowns go better fed.   #funny
? tier>=friend place:lounge
- One more song, then bed. You've a test.   #warm
- Raise a cup, everyone. Tier 3 tomorrow.   #warm

== pu3.watch
? dept:works
- Don't mind us. We're just passing. Slowly.   #funny
- Steady. Check it's dead before you touch it.
- Calder's quiet. Quiet's good with Calder.   #funny
?
- That's the shutdown test, isn't it? Good luck.
- Lights going off for the test? Fine by me.

== pu3.passed
? tier>=friend
- How did it go? Your face says well. Does it?   #warm
- Result tomorrow? I'll be outside the glass.   #warm
- You passed. I know you passed. Tell me tomorrow.   #funny
?
- Heard the junction came back on first time.
- Your Tier 3 test's done? That's a big one.
? dept:works
- Clean shutdown today. Nobody even spilt a tea.
- The bay's talking about your junction. Good talk.
- Calder said "Good." Twice, apparently.   #funny

== pu3.senior
? tier>=friend
- Senior Officer! At this rate you'll be Captain.   #funny
- Senior Officer. I knew it. I'm so pleased.   #warm
- The bar this afternoon? I'm coming. Try and stop me.   #warm
?
- Congratulations, Senior Officer.
- Senior Officer already? Well done.
- The Captain pins your bar at half four, I hear.
? dept:works
- A Senior in the bay. Mind you still make the tea.   #funny
- Tier 3 jobs on the board for you now. Lucky you.   #funny
? act:breakfast|dinner
- That's the new Senior Officer. Over there.

== pu3.bar.friend
? tier>=friend
- Senior Officer. Look at you. Look at the bar.   #warm
- It's straight. I checked. Calder checked too.   #funny
- Well done. Properly. I'm so proud of you.   #warm
?
- Congratulations. Suits you.

== pu3.cake
? tier>=friend
- Brennan made it for you. So you get the corner.   #warm
- First slice is yours. Second's mine. That's the rule.   #funny
?
- Cake for the new Senior. Lovely.

// one of the two people you warn in the test ({room} if the builder fills it; these never need it)
== pu3.warned
- A shutdown? Thanks for telling me. I'll go elsewhere.
- How long? An hour? Fine. Thanks for the warning.
- Right you are. I'll save my work first.
- Off at ten? I'll take my tea break then. Thanks.
- Thank you for coming to say. Most people don't.
- Fine. Shout when it's back on, will you?
? dept:works
- Shutting it down? Good. That breaker's been noisy.
- I'll keep clear. Gloves on, you.
? dept:command
- Noted. I'll let the bridge know. Thank you.
? dept:galley
- Off? Not the ovens, I hope. No? Then that's fine.
? dept:survey
- I'll back my readings up first. Thank you.

// Mail from up to two friends the day you're made Senior Officer ("Subject | body", {me} and {nick})
== mail.pu3.friend
? tier=friend
- Senior Officer! | Heard at lunch. Senior Officer {me}. You'll need a bigger mug. Come and find me later.   #funny
- Well done | Two promotions in a month. I've had one in two years. Well done, properly. Tea soon?   #warm
? tier=close
- Told you, again | I said you'd make Senior. I was right again. I'm getting used to it. So proud of you.   #warm
- Your bar | I want to see the bar up close. I'll be at the observation room door. Congratulations, {nick}.   #warm
